      "widgets_values": [
        "## People video (Wan 2.2 14B)\n\nAnimates a photo into a short silent clip with Wan 2.2's 14B image-to-video model. Much better at keeping the\nperson, clothing and style intact than the 5B workflow, and slower.\n\n1. Pick the photo. It is the first frame; the video keeps its shape (portrait stays portrait).\n2. Describe the motion in the prompt (below), then **Run**.\n3. The clip is saved to `ComfyUI/output` as `people_video_wan14b_00001_.mp4` (16 fps).\n\n### How it works\nWan 2.2 14B is two models: a *high noise* expert lays out the motion, a *low noise* expert fills in detail.\nBoth are GGUF-quantized (needs the **ComfyUI-GGUF** custom node) and use the lightx2v 4-step LoRAs: 2 steps\neach instead of 20, at cfg 1.\n\n### Prompt tips\n- Describe one or two simple actions: a smile, a head turn, a wave, a laugh, hair moving in the wind.\n- Say what stays the same (face, hair, clothing, background).\n- Add camera direction: *steady camera*, *slow push-in*, *gentle pan left*.\n- The negative prompt (Chinese, from the official template) does little at cfg 1; leave it alone.\n\n### Settings\n- **short_edge**: 480 (default). 720 is sharper and roughly 2½× slower.\n- **duration**: seconds (3 by default; up to 5 s is the trained range). Time grows faster than length.\n- **noise_seed** (first sampler): change it for a different take of the same prompt.\n\n### Timing (M5 Pro, 832×480, models already loaded)\n- Portrait 480×640, 3 s (the default): about 3½ min.\n- Landscape 832×480: 2 s in about 3 min, 5 s in about 8½ min.\n- The first run of a session adds a minute or so while the models load.\n- Memory: it uses most of a 48 GB Mac (macOS swaps up to ~20 GB); close big apps first. If it thrashes, switch both\n  loaders to the Q6_K files (12 GB each instead of 15.4, about as fast, very close in quality).\n- On macOS `run.sh` adds `--gpu-only`, which helps image edits but makes this ~12% slower; start ComfyUI with\n  `COMFYUI_GPU_ONLY=0 ./run.sh` for video sessions.\n\nModels are in the Model Links note. Missing? Extensions → *Download missing models to server*."
      ],
      "title": "Note: How to use"
    },
